Subject: [PATCH 06/49] Plutonium: panel tab keys, new browser tab, app
 launcher
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Alt+1…9 focus the right panel's tab at that position, Ctrl+Tab and
Ctrl+Shift+Tab cycle them, Ctrl+T opens a browser tab with its address bar
focused, and Super+Space opens an app launcher (a command palette mode)
that starts a desktop app in the current thread and opens its window as a
focused panel tab. In the Plutonium shell these are registered as shell
shortcuts, so they also work while an app or browser tab has the keyboard.

